  "id": "Compound::DB01364 - Gene::148",
  "verbalization": "Ephedrine is implicated in the relationship with Adra1a through a shared pathway involving pseudoephedrine, an adrenergic agonist. The evidence suggests that Ephedrine causes prostatic hypertrophy, acute retention of urine, and prostatism, all of which are linked to pseudoephedrine. Pseudoephedrine binds to Adra1a, indicating a direct interaction between the two entities. The lowest common ancestor of Ephedrine and pseudoephedrine points to the adrenergic agonist class, reinforcing the connection between Ephedrine and Adra1a through a common mechanism. The consistent presence of pseudoephedrine as a mediator in multiple pathways supports a role for Adra1a in the effects of Ephedrine. The evidence suggests that Ephedrine may act through pseudoephedrine to modulate Adra1a, potentially influencing physiological processes through adrenergic signaling.",
